  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=\\frac{10}{2}=5\\,\\text{in}$ and $h=8\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV=\\pi (5)^{2}(8)=200\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
